{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794784412,"nonce":"OI/dU42BIRgPUvk9HCZH6Vx0MHU=","message":"Diagnosis (harness scene with header/footer; NO_GUARD and VARIANT=stack/scroll local switches):\n\n1. Images: element collection folded any sharp clip inside a scroll container (a stack layer) into the image's scroll_clip, which rows hold with the viewport. Fixed in the commit citing this issue: only a sharp scroll container's clip goes into scroll_clip; everything else intersects into the primary clip. Stack variant dropped from ~5000 px to 71 px.\n\n2. Root cause of the rest: a primitive has one clip rect. On rows, a clip introduced inside the moved content is intersected at paint with the scroll viewport and then moved whole (clip_from). Content painted in the overscan band, cut by the viewport, stays cut when it scrolls into view (row 0's status dot and nested scroll text vanish); content painted inside and moved out is not cut by the viewport any more (draws over the header/footer: 709 px in the nested-scroll variant).\n\nDesign for the fix: keep the static part and the moving part apart. At slot time, for a primitive whose clip was introduced inside slot s: clip_bounds = ambient(s) (stays); the inner part becomes a path clip (rounded-rect shape block appended to the batch's aux rows) that follows the rows from s via clip_shape.y, which the shaders already take back through the rows. Edges of the clip that coincide with ambient(s) are extended outward (the viewport cut them, or they coincide with it). A primitive that already has a path clip, or a non-uniform radius, declines. Text primitives need the same (text batch aux rows; text.rs path test without the row mapping). Images in a nested scroll keep a scroll_clip that holds the outer viewport ∩ inner viewport and need the same split.\n\nAlso found: when rows decline because of an image at paint, the `patched == false` path clears cached_motion_subtree_images, the adopt call then gets images None, rows apply without the image list and the images are not drawn by any pass afterwards. Declining for images is therefore not safe today.\n\nRemaining guard stays until the above lands.","files":null}]}